OL,3,GNEWSAPlastic pellet clean-up resumes on
OL,4,Abeach
OL,5,
OL,6,FWork to remove millions of plastic
OL,7,Fpellets from a beach following a leak
OL,8,Fat a wastewater plant has resumed
OL,9,Ffollowing a break over the summer.
OL,11,FMillions of pellets, known as biobeads,
OL,12,Fentered the sea after a spill at a
OL,13,FSouthern Water treatment works in
OL,14,FEastbourne in October 2025, before
OL,15,Fwashing up in Camber Sands and Rye
OL,16,FHarbour Nature Reserve in East Sussex,
OL,17,Fand St Mary's Bay in Kent.
OL,19,FA clean-up operation had been in place
OL,20,Fsince November, but was put on hold in
OL,21,FCamber during the summer months due to
OL,22,Fthe beach's popularity.
OL,23,APub: 12-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,330,320,200,140,0,100
